<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Little Entente</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Little Entente was an alliance formed in 1920–1921 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, with the backing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its aim was to prevent Hungarian revision of the post-war frontiers and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> restoration and to defend the settlement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a>. It weakened in the 1930s with the rise of Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a> of 1938.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/little-entente.jpg" alt="Little Entente" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tschechoslowakei · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Little_Entente_in_Europe_1921-1938.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
